    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o-2026-06-23T08:37:50.180366+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T08:37:50.180366+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The 2007 paper described a \"choose your own adventure\" model of learning — one where students follow tangents, pursue what interests them, and encounter core curriculum concepts through the side doors of genuine curiosity rather than the front door of instruction. The paper acknowledged this was \"somewhat chaotic\" and that it would require new kinds of instructional design, new assessment tools, and teachers willing to trade some control for authentic engagement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "Translated Output:\nO artigo de 2007 descreveu um modelo de aprendizagem \"escolha seu próprio caminho\" - onde os alunos seguem tangentes, buscam o que lhes interessa e encontram conceitos do currículo principal através das portas laterais da curiosidade genuína em vez da porta da frente da instrução. O artigo reconheceu que isso era \"um pouco caótico\" e que exigiria novos tipos de design instrucional, novas ferramentas de avaliação e professores dispostos a trocar algum controle por engajamento autêntico.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o-2026-06-23T08:37:50.180366+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c-2026-06-23T08:43:59.940308+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T08:43:59.940308+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "Peripateticware doesn't fully solve the chaos — that tension is real and probably permanent. What it does is give teachers enough structure to stay sane (designed activities, learning targets, completion phases, teacher approval workflows) while giving students enough freedom to actually go somewhere (GPS-triggered content, student-proposed activities, self-directed field notes, peer projects)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "O software Peripateticware não resolve totalmente o caos - essa tensão é real e provavelmente permanente. O que ele faz é dar aos professores estrutura suficiente para se manterem sãos (atividades planejadas, metas de aprendizado, fases de conclusão, fluxo de aprovação do professor) enquanto dá aos alunos liberdade suficiente para realmente ir a algum lugar (conteúdo ativado por GPS, atividades propostas pelos alunos, anotações de campo autodirigidas, projetos entre pares).",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c-2026-06-23T08:43:59.940308+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c"
      }
    },
    {
